# Design Quality Rules

Before significant UI work, read `docs/DESIGN_SYSTEM.md`.

The visual concept is:

> After-class engineering at sunset.

The site must feel like an editorial engineering archive, not a SaaS template.

Prioritize:

- real project media;
- verified system diagrams;
- typography;
- asymmetric editorial composition;
- technical rules and labels;
- restrained sunset accents;
- project-specific visual logic;
- honest status and limitations.

Avoid:

- glowing gradient blobs;
- glassmorphism;
- excessive cards;
- universal bento grids;
- giant centered headline with a pill above it;
- fake browser windows;
- fake terminals;
- random 3D objects;
- technology marquees;
- fake metrics;
- meaningless motion;
- excessive `rounded-3xl`;
- startup copy;
- stock imagery;
- AI-generated project imagery.

Motion must explain state, hierarchy, or system flow and respect reduced motion.

At 320 px, 390 px, 768 px, 1024 px, and 1440 px:

- no horizontal overflow;
- no clipped headings;
- readable Korean;
- usable filters;
- intentional mobile composition.
